vacy standard  focus mostly on IT security and there's  12 control areas there and and we meet  all of those control areas and can make  this certificate available to customers  based upon that we built upon that and  we're able to service the healthcare  industry by by complying with HIPAA and  we comply with HIPAA and we'll meet the  contractual requirements by providing a  business associates agreement to covered  entities in the healthcare space I know  that sounds like a lot of gobbly [ __ ]  but what that means is is that if you're  if you are building a healthcare  application which has patient data in it  that data is covered by the HIPAA laws  and we can provide an environment that  enables customers to deliver those type  of applications but be sure that the  service provider us is making sure that  that data stays safe and private and  we're backing that up in the contract we  and in a very similar vein we support  PCI DSS which is the payment card  industry data security standard we've  certified the whole platform against  version 2 and the reason it's version 2  is at the time we started the audit on  that version 3 hadn't been ratified by  the payment card industry yet they did  that work and we actually have just  completed our 3.0 certification and  we're signing certificates right now so  we're very shortly in fact you're the  first people that are hearing this right  now because I got the email this morning  but we'll be making some noise about  that but so for for those Reap for those  folks in the retail industry and the  people in the banking in  the street that are dealing with payment  card data we provide this assurance that  that will safeguard that information as  well and they can use that to build up  their compliance story with their  auditors and with with their customers  that they need to do that with very  quickly FISMA FedRAMP these are US  federal government standards for  government to be able to take advantage  of information se